s they concern. Record every outside review, from another model, a blind reader, an estimator or a person, with life_review_record under its actual reviewer, and link later changes that answer it with answers. Before you report to the user, put every reason you give there into the graph: a later agent reads the graph, not your reply. To continue existing work, read life_construction_replay from the start at outline level, then life_model_outline, and open detail where you need it.\\n\\nThe author-model rules (life-sim://addon/storytelling, \\\"Model the author and its effect on prose\\\") apply when drafting and reviewing prose, not to this exploration.\",\"responseGuidance\":\"Briefly unpack the seed, then offer two or three names with the sound or meaning connection and their fit to the story. Flag confusion with existing names or a forced derivation; another draw is valid. Do not rename existing characters.\",\"generator\":\"calling_llm\",\"candidates\":null,\"advisoryOnly\":true,\"contextCompletenessVerified\":false,\"worldMutation\":false,\"graphMutation\":false,\"taskHash\":\"19114ca85d3a7328456ac7ea3c95adfbac9521b545bc7b2a4b7bee39c56b1426\"},\"alternatives\":[{\"name\":\"White Hart Building Society\",\"seedConnection\":\"Heart heard as hart, the deer; the White Hart is one of the commonest English inn names.\",\"fit\":\"Early building societies were founded in pubs; an invented society started in 1868 by railwaymen meeting at a White Hart inn would take the inn's name. Staff call it the Hart. Not the name of any building society the recorder knows of; the pub name is generic.\"},{\"name\":\"Hearth and Home Building Society\",\"seedConnection\":\"Heart to hearth: fire and home.\",\"fit\":\"Plausible Victorian phrasing, but reads like a slogan.\"},{\"name\":\"Heartland Building Society\",\"seedConnection\":\"The heart of the country.\",\"fit\":\"Sounds like a 1990s rebrand, not a Victorian mutual.\"}]},\"authoringClock\":{\"rootId\":\"story.understanding.c47836